   "licenseNote": "as stated in SuttaCentral publication metadata (bilara-data _publication-v2.json); the translator additionally requests that use not be for AI training datasets, AI models or AI-derived technologies",
   "lines": [
    {
     "n": 1,
     "text": "A liar goes to hell,"
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "text": "as does one who denies what they did."
    },
    {
     "n": 3,
     "text": "Both are equal in the hereafter,"
    },
    {
     "n": 4,
     "text": "those men of base deeds."
    },
    {
     "n": 5,
     "text": "Many who wear a scrap of ocher cloth"
    },
    {
     "n": 6,
     "text": "are unrestrained and wicked."
    },
    {
     "n": 7,
     "text": "Being wicked, they are reborn in hell"
    },
    {
     "n": 8,
     "text": "due to their bad deeds."
    },
    {
     "n": 9,
     "text": "It’d be better for the immoral and unrestrained"
    },
    {
     "n": 10,
     "text": "to eat an iron ball,"
    },
    {
     "n": 11,
     "text": "scorching, like a burning flame,"
    },
    {
     "n": 12,
     "text": "than to eat the nation’s alms."
    },
    {
     "n": 13,
     "text": "Four things befall a heedless man"
    },
    {
     "n": 14,
     "text": "who sleeps with another’s wife:"
    },
    {
     "n": 15,
     "text": "wickedness, poor sleep,"
    },
    {
     "n": 16,
     "text": "ill-repute, and rebirth in hell."
    },
    {
     "n": 17,
     "text": "He accrues wickedness and is reborn in a bad place,"
    },
    {
     "n": 18,
     "text": "all so a frightened couple may snatch a moment’s pleasure,"
    },
    {
     "n": 19,
     "text": "for which rulers impose a heavy punishment."
    },
    {
     "n": 20,
     "text": "That’s why a man should not sleep with another’s wife."
    },
    {
     "n": 21,
     "text": "When kusa grass is wrongly grasped"
    },
    {
     "n": 22,
     "text": "it only cuts the hand."
    },
    {
     "n": 23,
     "text": "So too, the ascetic life, when wrongly taken,"
    },
    {
     "n": 24,
     "text": "drags you to hell."
    },
    {
     "n": 25,
     "text": "Any lax act,"
    },
    {
     "n": 26,
     "text": "any corrupt observance,"
    },
    {
     "n": 27,
     "text": "or suspicious spiritual life,"
    },
    {
     "n": 28,
     "text": "is not very fruitful."
    },
    {
     "n": 29,
     "text": "If one is to do what should be done,"
    },
    {
     "n": 30,
     "text": "one should staunchly strive."
    },
    {
     "n": 31,
     "text": "For the life gone forth when laxly led"
    },
    {
     "n": 32,
     "text": "just stirs up dust all the more."
    },
    {
     "n": 33,
     "text": "A bad deed is better left undone,"
    },
    {
     "n": 34,
     "text": "for it will plague you later on."
    },
    {
     "n": 35,
     "text": "A good deed is better done,"
    },
    {
     "n": 36,
     "text": "one that does not plague you."
    },
    {
     "n": 37,
     "text": "As a frontier city"
    },
    {
     "n": 38,
     "text": "is guarded inside and out,"
    },
    {
     "n": 39,
     "text": "so you should ward yourselves—"
    },
    {
     "n": 40,
     "text": "don’t let the moment pass you by."
    },
    {
     "n": 41,
     "text": "For if you miss your moment"
    },
    {
     "n": 42,
     "text": "you’ll grieve when sent to hell."
    },
    {
     "n": 43,
     "text": "Unashamed of what is shameful,"
    },
    {
     "n": 44,
     "text": "ashamed of what is not shameful;"
    },
    {
     "n": 45,
     "text": "beings who uphold wrong view"
    },
    {
     "n": 46,
     "text": "go to a bad place."
    },
    {
     "n": 47,
     "text": "Seeing danger where there is none,"
    },
    {
     "n": 48,
     "text": "and blind to the actual danger,"
    },
    {
     "n": 49,
     "text": "beings who uphold wrong view"
    },
    {
     "n": 50,
     "text": "go to a bad place."
    },
    {
     "n": 51,
     "text": "Seeing fault where there is none,"
    },
    {
     "n": 52,
     "text": "and blind to the actual fault,"
    },
    {
     "n": 53,
     "text": "beings who uphold wrong view"
    },
    {
     "n": 54,
     "text": "go to a bad place."
    },
    {
     "n": 55,
     "text": "Knowing a fault as a fault"
    },
    {
     "n": 56,
     "text": "and the faultless as faultless,"
    },
    {
     "n": 57,
     "text": "beings who uphold right view"
    },
    {
     "n": 58,
     "text": "go to a good place."
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
